<li class="custom-item" id="06GM"><p>
 Categories cofibered in groupoids form a $(2, 1)$-category $\text{Cof}(\mathcal{C})$. Its 1-morphisms are the morphisms described in (<a href="/tag/06GL" data-tag="06GL">7</a>). If $p : \mathcal{F} \to C$ and $p': \mathcal{F}' \to \mathcal{C}$ are categories cofibered in groupoids and $\varphi , \psi : \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}'$ are $1$-morphisms, then a 2-morphism $t : \varphi \to \psi $ is a morphism of functors such that $p'(t_ x) = \text{id}_{p(x)}$ for all $x \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{F})$. 
</p>
</li>